# Application layer

## Use cases
- One file per command, in `application/commands/<command-name>.ts`.
- Export a curried function: `(deps) => async (input) => Promise<Result<Output, Error>>`.
- Validate inputs minimally (the Server Action did Zod validation already, here we adapt to domain VOs).
- Pattern: load aggregate via repo → call domain method → repo.save → return Result.
- NEVER call Supabase directly from a use case. Always through a repository port.

## Ports
- Interfaces in `application/ports/`. NO implementations here.
- Names end with `.repository.ts`, `.port.ts`, etc.

## Queries
- Read-only operations live in `application/queries/`. They MAY call Supabase directly via the server client (for reads that don't fit the aggregate, e.g. dashboard projections). Justified case-by-case.

## Errors
- Either return the domain `XError`, or `{ code: 'not_found' }`. Never invent new error shapes here.
